# Optional. PostHog project API key (public — safe to expose in a browser
# bundle). When set, posthog-js initialises once at app startup with exception
# autocapture only (errors + pageviews — no session recording, no heatmaps).
# Unset means no PostHog client is created at all. Shares the project with the
# server's POSTHOG_API_KEY (server/.env.example).
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_kA7kTxYi37zAcuoqaJ5rSjFLQfe3bvY2zkhP6ApqM2BS
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Baked in by the Docker build (Dockerfile ARG GIT_SHA) as the PostHog
# `release` tag on every captured exception. Not meant to be hand-set for a
# local dev server — leave unset there.
# VITE_GIT_SHA=
